      "text": "Wiederkehr Village takes its name from Swiss winemaker Johann Andreas Wiederkehr, who arrived in 1880.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiederkehr_Village%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded by the Wiederkehr family in the 1880s, the village keeps an old‑world feel with stone cellars, timbered buildings, lederhosen‑wearing servers, and hillside vineyards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansas.com/regions-cities/cities/wiederkehr-village",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "At this Alpine‑looking oasis, visitors learn the winery’s philosophy, tour the vineyard and hand‑dug cellar, and taste award‑winning wines at the on‑site Vintage 1880 Gift Shop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.islands.com/2164056/wiederkehr-village-arkansas-old-world-ozarks-european-style-getaway-wine/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town blends Ozark scenery with an old‑world European feel, where Swiss winemaking traditions meet Southern landscapes, offering a unique, affordable Alpine alternative.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.islands.com/2164056/wiederkehr-village-arkansas-old-world-ozarks-european-style-getaway-wine/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sitting on slopes above the Arkansas River Valley, Wiederkehr Village showcases Swiss winemaking traditions amid Southern scenery.",
